## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces

- New: one command, one API function, one schema, one reference page, one
  how-to, one example. `__all__` grows by one, appended.
- No change to the `check`, `witness` or `replay` contracts.
- Packaged skills: WN3-C4.

## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Why-not and `check` disagree on derivability | WN-R2 helper reuse; WN1-C2 agreement test on every corpus case |
| Declared order misleads when the evaluator reorders | Payload states the order used; WN-D2 ruling |
| Cross-product prefixes blow up | WN-R4 ceilings; WN1-C5 time-bound test |
| Values leak into logs | WN-R5 redaction default; WN2-C2 |
| "Blocked" read as "false" | Docs state why-not explains a missing derivation in this population; it proves nothing about the world |
| The kernel's test oracle shares code with it | Oracle is a separate naive evaluator with no import from `extensions` join helpers |
| Downstream names leak | O14; review lens |
| A repair round introduces defects | §8 round budget and stop rule |

## 7. Out of scope

- A field in the `check` report or any report schema bump (unless WN-D1 rules
  otherwise).
- The direct-derivation request (GR-T5) and the reporter's other requests.
- Automatic repair: GND names the gap; adding facts is the host's move.
- Explaining constraint violations (already reported by `check`).
- Aggregates and opaque rules (WN-D6), native, LQP and PyRel runtimes.
- Changes inside the downstream application. Publication, release,
  certification.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

`auto=false`. Each phase follows `process-phase`: spec, owner gate,
implementation and focused tests, one independent local diff reader, a
refactoring review and a record. No code is written before recorded spec
approval. Plan and close review instrument: WN-D8 `(o)`, four local readers
with lenses: correctness against production semantics; implementability;
protocol and anonymity; test design and falsifiability). One reader is one
reader, not a panel. Round budget: one review round over r1, then at most one
confirmation round over the blocking findings, then the stop rule in
`review-convergence.md`. Work happens on a topic branch, then a PR; merge
requires the owner.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Affected consumers and tests |
|---|---|---|
| WN1 | Kernel and oracle agree on the corpus; ceilings tested; no public diff | new kernel and oracle tests; `test_rf1_layering.py` |
| WN2 | Command and API exit as specified; schema validates; pins updated; check/witness parity | `test_public_api.py`, signature and runtime pins, witness corpus tests, docs link check |
| WN3 | Repair loop test passes end to end; docs build | example test, docs tests, skill census if a skill changes |

Exact focused gate commands are **unresolved** until each phase spec names
them. The broad suite runs on explicit owner selection.

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Proposed |
|---|---|---|---|
| WN-D1 | Surface | (a) new command + API in the witness lane; (b) a `check` report field: schema bump, cost on every check; (c) both | **(a)** |
| WN-D2 | Which order defines "first blocking atom" | (a) declaration-order prefixes: readable, stable, can enumerate a cross product; (b) the evaluator's reordered join: cheaper, but the "first" atom depends on connectivity and can differ from what the author reads | **(a)**, with the order named in the payload |
| WN-D3 | Descend into a derived blocking predicate | (a) no descent: the host sees a derived predicate and must ask again; (b) bounded descent when the atom grounds; (c) always descend over all bindings: unbounded | **(b)**, depth ceiling fixed in the WN1 spec |
| WN-D4 | Values in output | (a) redacted by default, `--raw` shows samples (as `witness`); (b) raw by default: the reporter needs the constants | **(a)**; the reporter passes `--raw` |
| WN-D5 | Exit bands | (a) `0` explained, `2` derived or unsupported, `3`, `4`; (b) `0` derived, `1` blocked: reads like a verdict, which WN-R1 forbids | **(a)** |
| WN-D6 | Supported fragment and ceilings | aggregates/opaque rules unsupported; reuse `WitnessLimits` or a sibling limits class | unsupported as listed; reuse `WitnessLimits` |
| WN-D7 | Code home | (a) `gnd.witness.why_not` in the witness lane; (b) a new `whynot` lane | **(a)**: shares input lane, limits, redaction |
| WN-D8 | Review instrument for plan and close | four local readers (as in recent milestones) or the maintained panel | **Ruled (o) 2026-10-30:** four local readers for plan and close; one reader per phase diff (proposed) |
| WN-D9 | Sample count for bound constants | how many bindings to show per blocker | 5, with the total count always given |

No open question is inherited from an earlier milestone. The issue's pin
(`8a3a98b`) is older than this baseline; nothing in its request depends on that
pin.
